title    Late Light
composer Claude
about    Eight bars of jazz ballad comping in Eb major. Sustained rootless voicings with smooth voice leading, over a two-feel upright and soft ride.
tempo    60      # slow ballad, one beat per second
beats    4
steps    2       # eighth notes are the finest rhythm needed
swing    0.3     # soft triplet lilt on the ride and the one anticipation

# Progression (one chord per bar unless noted):
# | Ebmaj9 | Cm9 | Fm9 | Bb13 | Abmaj9 | Gm9 C7b9 | Fm9 Bb13 | Eb6/9 |
# A I-vi-ii-V into IV, then a ii-V to the ii, and ii-V home: standard-ballad harmony.

# keys: the focus. Four-note rootless voicings (3rd/7th plus 9th/13th colors),
# because the bass carries the roots. They sit between D3 and G4, the warm middle
# of the piano, and each voice moves by step or common tone into the next chord.
# Bars 6-7 descend by half steps in every voice (C7b9 -> Fm9 -> Bb13).
# Rhythm is deliberately plain: chords on beat 1 (and 3 when the harmony changes)
# held long, so the ballad breathes. The only push is the Abmaj9 anticipated on
# the "and" of 4 in bar 4, which marks the arrival on the IV chord.
voice keys piano vol=0.75 pan=-0.15

# bass: half-note two-feel, root then fifth or a chromatic approach, so the
# rootless voicings have a clear foundation without busy motion.
voice bass upright vol=0.9 pan=0.1

# drums: very soft ride time plus hi-hat foot on 2 and 4, just enough pulse
# to hold the slow tempo together. No kick or snare to stay out of the way.
voice ride ride vol=0.35
voice hat hat vol=0.3

pattern A
keys | G3+Bb3+D4+F4------- | G3+Bb3+D4+Eb4------- | Ab3+C4+Eb4+G4------- | Ab3+C4+D4+G4----- . G3+Bb3+C4+Eb4 |
keys | = | F3+A3+Bb3+D4--- E3+A3+Bb3+Db4--- | Eb3+G3+Ab3+C4--- D3+G3+Ab3+C4--- | G3+Bb3+C4+F4------- |
bass | Eb2--- Bb1--- | C2--- G1--- | F1--- C2--- | Bb1--- A1--- |
bass | Ab1--- Eb2--- | G1--- C2--- | F1--- Bb1--- | Eb2--- Bb1--- |
ride | x.xx x.xx | % | % | % | % | % | % | % |
hat  | ..x. ..x. | % | % | % | % | % | % | % |

loop A
